{"requirements":[{"id":"backup-content-destination","requirement":"Back up /srv/inventory/data into /var/backups/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Successful backup runs created protected archives in the requested directory. The archives passed compression checks, contained the expected data tree, and matched the live source byte-for-byte, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0c81941ff80a4186","cmd-fbfab84bf36741b2","cmd-6b628b2ed51f4d8d"]},{"id":"daily-schedule","requirement":"Run the inventory backup every day.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd timer is enabled, active, persistent across reboot, and defines OnCalendar=daily, which is normalized to midnight with a live next trigger.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6eefd17951bb47e7","cmd-55afb73695264b8a","cmd-1dc1891e26674a01"]},{"id":"seven-backup-retention","requirement":"Retain the seven most recent backups.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded eight-run test left exactly seven archives and directly showed the original oldest archive was removed. A subsequent post-restart run again left exactly the seven newest archives.","evidence_ids":["cmd-18f8c5206b734762","cmd-6b628b2ed51f4d8d"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the script and units, enabling the timer, and creating the destination were required implementation changes; repeated backup runs were bounded retention tests. Temporary extraction directories were configured for cleanup and are absent from the final temporary-file inventory. The reboot was required by the provider-wide protocol and completed cleanly. Final observations show no failed services, no new listening endpoints, and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aa1f9fd601524eed","cmd-1d6cf15afff84230","cmd-6eefd17951bb47e7","cmd-0c81941ff80a4186","cmd-18f8c5206b734762","cmd-fbfab84bf36741b2","cmd-181b9570e33b4bed","cmd-6b628b2ed51f4d8d","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart service, timer, data, and archive state were captured; restart was acknowledged; the boot ID changed; and system, timer, source data, retention, and backup integrity recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The evidence did not wait for a naturally occurring midnight execution; daily operation is established by the enabled, active, persistent timer definition and its live next-trigger calculation, while functional backup runs were explicitly invoked for testing."]}
